@@@!atrep-exo
@=at-markdown=>md

@@/ Standard-library Markdown exomorphosis for at-markdown.
@@/ Every block rule's rendered value ends with exactly one line
@@/ break; the block join supplies the separating blank line.

@%
\ \\
` \`
* \*
_ \_
# \#
> \>
- \-
%@

@-> *document
@(grammata)
>-@

@-> *paragraph
@(grammata)

>-@

@@/ An autolink's target is read without backslash processing,
@@/ so it is written raw.
@-> ><
<@((grammata))>
>-@

@-> #
# @(grammata)
>-@

@-> ##
## @(grammata)
>-@

@-> ###
### @(grammata)
>-@

@-> ####
#### @(grammata)
>-@

@-> #####
##### @(grammata)
>-@

@-> ######
###### @(grammata)
>-@

@-> *
*@(grammata)*
>-@

@-> **
**@(grammata)**
>-@

@-> >
> @(grammata:> )
>-@

@-> -
- @(grammata:  )
>-@

@@/ Continuation lines hang under four spaces: enough for a
@@/ two-digit marker, and within the content column plus three
@@/ that a one-digit marker tolerates.
@-> .
@(taxis). @(grammata:    )
>-@

@-> *verbatim
```@((genoses))
@((content))```

>-@

@-> *verbatim-inline
`@((content))`
>-@

@-> *media
![](@((param)))

>-@

@@/ The footnote extension: the callout is a deixis, the body a
@@/ para-simmere on the same symbol. The label is an identifier,
@@/ written verbatim; continuation lines of a multi-paragraph
@@/ body indent four spaces.
@-> *deixis ^
[^@((onym))]
>-@

@-> ^
[^@((onym))]: @(grammata:    )
>-@

@-> *onym-anchor
>-@
